# Settings for swift-app-kit's setup.sh. It reads this with bash, so quote values.

APP_NAME="Snap"
BUNDLE_ID="local.snap"
SYMBOL="rectangle.split.2x2"
ICON_TOP="0.20 0.80 0.62"
ICON_BOTTOM="0.05 0.52 0.78"
INSTALL_NOTES="Look for the grid icon in the menu bar.

  • The first time, macOS asks you to allow Snap in Accessibility settings. Snap needs that to
    move windows. Turn it on in System Settings → Privacy & Security → Accessibility.
  • Then try ⌃⌥← and ⌃⌥→ on any window. ⌃⌥↑ then ⌃⌥→ in quick succession makes a quarter.
  • Snap starts automatically at login. Change shortcuts and other options in Settings…"
